:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDAJE.Add Autostart Job Entry (ADDAJE)
:P.Use the Add Autostart Job Entry (ADDAJE) command to add an autostart
job entry to a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDAJE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDAJE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDAJE/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDJOBQE.Add Job Queue Entry (ADDJOBQE)
:P.Use the Add Job Queue Entry (ADDJOBQE) command to add a job queue
entry to a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXACT'.Maximum active jobs (MAXACT)
:P.The most jobs or routing steps that can be active at once. *NOMAX
sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY1'.Max active priority 1 (MAXPTY1)
:P.The max active priority 1 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY2'.Max active priority 2 (MAXPTY2)
:P.The max active priority 2 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY3'.Max active priority 3 (MAXPTY3)
:P.The max active priority 3 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY4'.Max active priority 4 (MAXPTY4)
:P.The max active priority 4 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY5'.Max active priority 5 (MAXPTY5)
:P.The max active priority 5 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY6'.Max active priority 6 (MAXPTY6)
:P.The max active priority 6 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY7'.Max active priority 7 (MAXPTY7)
:P.The max active priority 7 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY8'.Max active priority 8 (MAXPTY8)
:P.The max active priority 8 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBQE/MAXPTY9'.Max active priority 9 (MAXPTY9)
:P.The max active priority 9 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDJOBSCDE.Add Job Schedule Entry (ADDJOBSCDE)
:P.Use the Add Job Schedule Entry (ADDJOBSCDE) command to add an entry
to the job schedule.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/CMD'.Command to run (CMD)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/FRQ'.Frequency (FRQ)
:P.The frequency for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WEEKLY:EPK.
:PD.Weekly.
:PT.:PK.*MONTHLY:EPK.
:PD.Monthly.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ONCE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/SCDDATE'.Schedule date (SCDDATE)
:P.The date the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MONTHSTR, *MONTHEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/SCDDAY'.Schedule day (SCDDAY)
:P.The schedule day for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU, *FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/SCDTIME'.Schedule time (SCDTIME)
:P.The time the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/RELDAYMON'.Relative day of month (RELDAYMON)
:P.The relative day of month for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 5.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/SAVE'.Save (SAVE)
:P.Whether to save.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/OMITDATE'.Omit date (OMITDATE)
:P.The omit date for this command.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/RCYACN'.Recovery action (RCYACN)
:P.The recovery action for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SBMRLS, *SBMHLD, *NOSBM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.No message queue&colon. messages are not sent.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDJOBSCDE/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDLIBLE.Add Library List Entry (ADDLIBLE)
:P.Use the Add Library List Entry (ADDLIBLE) command to add a library to
the user part of the library list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLIBLE/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLIBLE/POSITION'.Library list position (POSITION)
:P.The library list position for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. List position
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*BEFORE:EPK.
:PD.Before the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Reference library
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDPJE.Add Prestart Job Entry (ADDPJE)
:P.Use the Add Prestart Job Entry (ADDPJE) command to add a prestart job
entry to a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/USER'.User profile (USER)
:P.The user profile for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QUSER is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/STRJOBS'.Start jobs (STRJOBS)
:P.Whether to start jobs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/INLJOBS'.Initial number of jobs (INLJOBS)
:P.The initial number of jobs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 3 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/THRESHOLD'.Threshold (THRESHOLD)
:P.The threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 2 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/ADLJOBS'.Additional number of jobs (ADLJOBS)
:P.The additional number of jobs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 2 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/MAXJOBS'.Maximum number of jobs (MAXJOBS)
:P.The most jobs allowed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/MAXUSE'.Maximum number of uses (MAXUSE)
:P.The maximum number of uses for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 200 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/WAIT'.Wait for job (WAIT)
:P.Whether to wait for job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/POOLID'.Pool identifier (POOLID)
:P.The subsystem pool identifier.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Class
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Number of jobs to use class
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/THDRSCAFN'.Thread resources affinity (THDRSCAFN)
:P.Whether the job's secondary threads are kept close to the processors
and memory the first thread uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Group
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOGROUP, *GROUP.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPJE/RSCAFNGRP'.Resources affinity group (RSCAFNGRP)
:P.Whether the job's threads are kept together on the same processor
group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDRTGE.Add Routing Entry (ADDRTGE)
:P.Use the Add Routing Entry (ADDRTGE) command to add a routing entry to
a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/SEQNBR'.Routing entry sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The routing entry sequence number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/CMPVAL'.Comparison data (CMPVAL)
:P.The comparison data for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Compare value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 80 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Starting position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 80.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/PGM'.Program to call (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SBSD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the subsystem description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/MAXACT'.Maximum active routing steps (MAXACT)
:P.The most jobs or routing steps that can be active at once. *NOMAX
sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/POOLID'.Storage pool identifier (POOLID)
:P.The subsystem pool identifier.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/THDRSCAFN'.Thread resources affinity (THDRSCAFN)
:P.Whether the job's secondary threads are kept close to the processors
and memory the first thread uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Group
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOGROUP, *GROUP.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRTGE/RSCAFNGRP'.Resources affinity group (RSCAFNGRP)
:P.Whether the job's threads are kept together on the same processor
group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDWSE.Add Work Station Entry (ADDWSE)
:P.Use the Add Work Station Entry (ADDWSE) command to add a workstation
entry, by name or by type, to a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDWSE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDWSE/WRKSTN'.Work station name (WRKSTN)
:P.The work station name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDWSE/WRKSTNTYPE'.Work station type (WRKSTNTYPE)
:P.The work station type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NONASCII.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDWSE/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SBSD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the subsystem description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDWSE/MAXACT'.Maximum active jobs (MAXACT)
:P.The most jobs or routing steps that can be active at once. *NOMAX
sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDWSE/AT'.Allocation (AT)
:P.The allocation for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ENTER:EPK.
:PD.Enter.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIGNON.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGBCKUP.Change Backup Options (CHGBCKUP)
:P.Use the Change Backup Options (CHGBCKUP) command to change what a
backup saves and where.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGBCKUP/BCKUPOPT'.Backup options (BCKUPOPT)
:P.The backup options of the operational assistant&colon. daily, weekly
or monthly.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WEEKLY:EPK.
:PD.Weekly.
:PT.:PK.*MONTHLY:EPK.
:PD.Monthly.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DAILY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGBCKUP/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGBCKUP/TAPSET'.Tape set (TAPSET)
:P.The tape set for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
