:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCLNUP.Change Cleanup (CHGCLNUP)
:P.Use the Change Cleanup (CHGCLNUP) command to change the cleanup
options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/ALWCLNUP'.Allow cleanup (ALWCLNUP)
:P.The allow cleanup for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/STRTIME'.Time cleanup starts each day (STRTIME)
:P.The time cleanup starts each day for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SCDPWROFF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/USRMSG'.Number of days to keep (USRMSG)
:P.The number of days to keep for this command.
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. User messages
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/SYSMSG'.System and workstation msgs (SYSMSG)
:P.The system and workstation msgs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/CRITSYSMSG'.Critical system messages (CRITSYSMSG)
:P.The critical system messages for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/SYSPRT'.Job logs and system output (SYSPRT)
:P.The job logs and system output for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/SYSLOG'.System journals and logs (SYSLOG)
:P.The system journals and logs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/JRNRCVSIZ'.Journal receiver size (JRNRCVSIZ)
:P.The journal receiver size for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/CALITM'.Office calendar items (CALITM)
:P.The office calendar items for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLNUP/RUNPTY'.Run priority (RUNPTY)
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCLS.Change Class (CHGCLS)
:P.Use the Change Class (CHGCLS) command to change a class.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/RUNPTY'.Run priority (RUNPTY)
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/TIMESLICE'.Time slice (TIMESLICE)
:P.How long, in milliseconds, a thread of the job runs before another
thread of the same priority gets the processor.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 8 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/PURGE'.Eligible for purge (PURGE)
:P.Whether the job may be moved out of main storage when it waits for a
long time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/DFTWAIT'.Default wait time (DFTWAIT)
:P.How many seconds the system waits for an instruction to complete
before it signals a time-out.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/CPUTIME'.Maximum CPU time (CPUTIME)
:P.The maximum CPU time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/MAXTMPSTG'.Maximum temporary storage (MAXTMPSTG)
:P.The maximum temporary storage for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/MAXTHD'.Maximum threads (MAXTHD)
:P.The maximum threads for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCLS/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCURLIB.Change Current Library (CHGCURLIB)
:P.Use the Change Current Library (CHGCURLIB) command to change the
current library of the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCURLIB/CURLIB'.Current library (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CRTDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGIPLA.Change IPL Attributes (CHGIPLA)
:P.Use the Change IPL Attributes (CHGIPLA) command to change the
attributes the next IPL uses.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/RESTART'.Restart type (RESTART)
:P.The restart type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/KEYLCKPOS'.Keylock position (KEYLCKPOS)
:P.The keylock position for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MANUAL, *SECURE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/HDWDIAG'.Hardware diagnostics (HDWDIAG)
