:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/CHKJOBTBL'.Check job tables (CHKJOBTBL)
:P.The check job tables for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ABNORMAL, *SYNC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/RBDPRDDIR'.Rebuild product directory (RBDPRDDIR)
:P.The rebuild product directory for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ABNORMAL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/MSFRCY'.Mail Server Framework recovery (MSFRCY)
:P.The mail Server Framework recovery for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/DSPSTS'.Display status (DSPSTS)
:P.The display status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/STRTCP'.Start TCP/IP (STRTCP)
:P.The start TCP/IP for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/SPLFRCY'.Spooled file recovery (SPLFRCY)
:P.The spooled file recovery for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DETACH:EPK.
:PD.Detached from the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REMOVE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/CLRJOBQ'.Clear job queues (CLRJOBQ)
:P.The clear job queues for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/CLROUTQ'.Clear output queues (CLROUTQ)
:P.The clear output queues for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/CLRINCJOB'.Clear incomplete joblogs (CLRINCJOB)
:P.The clear incomplete joblogs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/STRPRTWTR'.Start print writers (STRPRTWTR)
:P.The start print writers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIPLA/STRRSTD'.Start to restricted state (STRRSTD)
:P.The start to restricted state for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGJOB.Change Job (CHGJOB)
:P.Use the Change Job (CHGJOB) command to change the attributes of a
job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/JOBPTY'.Job priority (on JOBQ) (JOBPTY)
:P.The priority of the job on the job queue, from 1 (highest) to 9
(lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/OUTPTY'.Output priority (on OUTQ) (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/PRTDEV'.Print device (PRTDEV)
:P.The printer device the spooled output prints on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/RUNPTY'.Run priority (RUNPTY)
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/LOG'.Message logging (LOG)
:P.The message logging for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 4.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Severity
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Text
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/LOGCLPGM'.Log CL program commands (LOGCLPGM)
:P.Whether the commands that CL programs run are written to the job log.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/LOGOUTPUT'.Log output (LOGOUTPUT)
:P.When the job log is produced as a spooled file&colon. by the job
itself at its end, by a server job afterwards, or not at all.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBLOGSVR, *JOBEND, *PND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/JOBMSGQFL'.Job message queue full action (JOBMSGQFL)
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NOWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, no more messages are added.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*PRTWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the messages are printed and the queue starts over.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/INQMSGRPY'.Inquiry message reply (INQMSGRPY)
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYSRPYL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/BRKMSG'.Break message handling (BRKMSG)
:P.The break message handling for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*NOTIFY:EPK.
:PD.The user is notified that a message arrived.
:PT.:PK.*HOLD:EPK.
:PD.Held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/STSMSG'.Status message (STSMSG)
:P.The status message for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DDMCNV'.DDM conversation (DDMCNV)
:P.Whether conversations to remote systems for DDM are kept or dropped
when nothing is using them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DROP:EPK.
:PD.Dropped.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/SCDDATE'.Schedule date (SCDDATE)
:P.The date the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MONTHSTR, *MONTHEND, *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU,
*FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/SCDTIME'.Schedule time (SCDTIME)
:P.The time the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DATE'.Job date (DATE)
:P.The job date.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DATFMT'.Date format (DATFMT)
:P.The format of dates&colon. the order of year, month and day.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*YMD:EPK.
:PD.Year, month, day.
:PT.:PK.*MDY:EPK.
:PD.Month, day, year.
:PT.:PK.*DMY:EPK.
:PD.Day, month, year.
:PT.:PK.*JUL:EPK.
:PD.Julian&colon. year and day of the year.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DATSEP'.Date separator (DATSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a date.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/TIMSEP'.Time separator (TIMSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DECFMT'.Decimal format (DECFMT)
:P.The decimal format&colon. the character used for the decimal point
and how zeros print before it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be I, J.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/SWS'.Job switches (SWS)
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/TIMESLICE'.Time slice (TIMESLICE)
:P.How long, in milliseconds, a thread of the job runs before another
thread of the same priority gets the processor.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 8 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/PURGE'.Eligible for purge (PURGE)
:P.Whether the job may be moved out of main storage when it waits for a
long time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DFTWAIT'.Default wait time (DFTWAIT)
:P.How many seconds the system waits for an instruction to complete
before it signals a time-out.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DEVRCYACN'.Device recovery action (DEVRCYACN)
:P.What happens to the job when its display device has an error&colon. a
message is sent, the request is ended, or the job is ended.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DSCMSG, *DSCENDRQS, *ENDJOB, *ENDJOBNOLIST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/TSEPOOL'.Time slice end pool (TSEPOOL)
:P.Whether the job moves to the base pool when its time slice ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/PRTKEYFMT'.Print key format (PRTKEYFMT)
:P.The print key format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRTBDR, *PRTHDR, *PRTALL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/CNTRYID'.Country or region ID (CNTRYID)
:P.The country or region identifier&colon. two letters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/CHRIDCTL'.Character identifier control (CHRIDCTL)
:P.How the character identifier of display and printer files is
handled&colon. the device's or the job's CCSID.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/SPLFACN'.Spooled file action (SPLFACN)
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DETACH:EPK.
:PD.Detached from the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOB/DUPJOBOPT'.Duplicate job option (DUPJOBOPT)
:P.What happens when more than one job matches the name given&colon.
show a list to choose from, or send a message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGJOBD.Change Job Description (CHGJOBD)
:P.Use the Change Job Description (CHGJOBD) command to change a job
description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/JOBPTY'.Job priority (on JOBQ) (JOBPTY)
:P.The priority of the job on the job queue, from 1 (highest) to 9
(lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/OUTPTY'.Output priority (on OUTQ) (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/PRTDEV'.Print device (PRTDEV)
:P.The printer device the spooled output prints on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/ACGCDE'.Accounting code (ACGCDE)
:P.The accounting code the job's resources are charged to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/RTGDTA'.Routing data (RTGDTA)
:P.The routing data the subsystem compares with its routing entries to
choose the program the job runs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 80 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RQSDTA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/RQSDTA'.Request data (RQSDTA)
:P.The request data placed on the job's message queue for the program to
read.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/SYNTAX'.CL syntax check severity (SYNTAX)
:P.The CL syntax check severity for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCHK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/INLLIBL'.Initial library list (INLLIBL)
:P.The initial user part of the library list of the job.
:P.Up to 250 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/ENDSEV'.End severity (ENDSEV)
:P.The end severity for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/LOG'.Message logging (LOG)
:P.The message logging for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 4.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Severity
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Text
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/LOGCLPGM'.Log CL program commands (LOGCLPGM)
:P.Whether the commands that CL programs run are written to the job log.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/LOGOUTPUT'.Log output (LOGOUTPUT)
:P.When the job log is produced as a spooled file&colon. by the job
itself at its end, by a server job afterwards, or not at all.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBLOGSVR, *JOBEND, *PND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/INQMSGRPY'.Inquiry message reply (INQMSGRPY)
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYSRPYL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/HOLD'.Hold on job queue (HOLD)
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It is not held.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/DATE'.Job date (DATE)
:P.The job date.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/SWS'.Job switches (SWS)
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/JOBMSGQMX'.Job message queue maximum (JOBMSGQMX)
:P.The largest size of the job's message queue, in megabytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 2 to 64.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/JOBMSGQFL'.Job message queue full action (JOBMSGQFL)
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NOWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, no more messages are added.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*PRTWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the messages are printed and the queue starts over.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/DEVRCYACN'.Device recovery action (DEVRCYACN)
:P.What happens to the job when its display device has an error&colon. a
message is sent, the request is ended, or the job is ended.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DSCMSG, *DSCENDRQS, *ENDJOB, *ENDJOBNOLIST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/TSEPOOL'.Time slice end pool (TSEPOOL)
:P.Whether the job moves to the base pool when its time slice ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/SPLFACN'.Spooled file action (SPLFACN)
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DETACH:EPK.
:PD.Detached from the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/DDMCNV'.DDM conversation (DDMCNV)
:P.Whether conversations to remote systems for DDM are kept or dropped
when nothing is using them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DROP:EPK.
:PD.Dropped.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBD/ALWMLTTHD'.Allow multiple threads (ALWMLTTHD)
:P.The allow multiple threads for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGJOBQ.Change Job Queue (CHGJOBQ)
:P.Use the Change Job Queue (CHGJOBQ) command to change a job queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQ/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQ/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQ/AUTCHK'.Authority to check (AUTCHK)
:P.Which authority is checked&colon. the owner's, or data authority.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAAUT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQ/OPRCTL'.Operator controlled (OPRCTL)
:P.Whether users with job control special authority can control the
queue.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGJOBQE.Change Job Queue Entry (CHGJOBQE)
:P.Use the Change Job Queue Entry (CHGJOBQE) command to change a job
queue entry of a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXACT'.Maximum active jobs (MAXACT)
:P.The most jobs or routing steps that can be active at once. *NOMAX
sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY1'.Max active priority 1 (MAXPTY1)
:P.The max active priority 1 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY2'.Max active priority 2 (MAXPTY2)
:P.The max active priority 2 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY3'.Max active priority 3 (MAXPTY3)
:P.The max active priority 3 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY4'.Max active priority 4 (MAXPTY4)
:P.The max active priority 4 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY5'.Max active priority 5 (MAXPTY5)
:P.The max active priority 5 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY6'.Max active priority 6 (MAXPTY6)
:P.The max active priority 6 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY7'.Max active priority 7 (MAXPTY7)
:P.The max active priority 7 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY8'.Max active priority 8 (MAXPTY8)
:P.The max active priority 8 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBQE/MAXPTY9'.Max active priority 9 (MAXPTY9)
:P.The max active priority 9 for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGJOBSCDE.Change Job Schedule Entry (CHGJOBSCDE)
:P.Use the Change Job Schedule Entry (CHGJOBSCDE) command to change an
entry of the job schedule.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/ENTRYNBR'.Entry number (ENTRYNBR)
:P.The entry number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/CMD'.Command to run (CMD)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *SAME is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/FRQ'.Frequency (FRQ)
:P.The frequency for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*WEEKLY:EPK.
:PD.Weekly.
:PT.:PK.*MONTHLY:EPK.
:PD.Monthly.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ONCE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/SCDDATE'.Schedule date (SCDDATE)
:P.The date the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MONTHSTR, *MONTHEND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/SCDDAY'.Schedule day (SCDDAY)
:P.The schedule day for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU, *FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/SCDTIME'.Schedule time (SCDTIME)
:P.The time the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/RELDAYMON'.Relative day of month (RELDAYMON)
:P.The relative day of month for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 5.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/SAVE'.Save (SAVE)
:P.The save for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/OMITDATE'.Omit date (OMITDATE)
:P.The omit date for this command.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/RCYACN'.Recovery action (RCYACN)
:P.The recovery action for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SBMRLS, *SBMHLD, *NOSBM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.No message queue&colon. messages are not sent.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGJOBSCDE/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGLIBL.Change Library List (CHGLIBL)
:P.Use the Change Library List (CHGLIBL) command to replace the user
part of the library list, and the current library if asked.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLIBL/LIBL'.Libraries for current thread (LIBL)
:P.The libraries for current thread for this command.
:P.Up to 250 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLIBL/CURLIB'.Current library (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CRTDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPJE.Change Prestart Job Entry (CHGPJE)
:P.Use the Change Prestart Job Entry (CHGPJE) command to change a
prestart job entry of a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/USER'.User profile (USER)
:P.The user profile for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/STRJOBS'.Start jobs (STRJOBS)
:P.The start jobs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/INLJOBS'.Initial number of jobs (INLJOBS)
:P.The initial number of jobs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/THRESHOLD'.Threshold (THRESHOLD)
:P.The threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/ADLJOBS'.Additional number of jobs (ADLJOBS)
:P.The additional number of jobs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/MAXJOBS'.Maximum number of jobs (MAXJOBS)
:P.The most jobs allowed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/MAXUSE'.Maximum number of uses (MAXUSE)
:P.The maximum number of uses for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/WAIT'.Wait for job (WAIT)
:P.The wait for job for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/POOLID'.Pool identifier (POOLID)
:P.The subsystem pool identifier.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Class
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Number of jobs to use class
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/THDRSCAFN'.Thread resources affinity (THDRSCAFN)
:P.Whether the job's secondary threads are kept close to the processors
and memory the first thread uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Group
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOGROUP, *GROUP.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPJE/RSCAFNGRP'.Resources affinity group (RSCAFNGRP)
:P.Whether the job's threads are kept together on the same processor
group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGRTGE.Change Routing Entry (CHGRTGE)
:P.Use the Change Routing Entry (CHGRTGE) command to change a routing
entry of a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/SEQNBR'.Routing entry sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The routing entry sequence number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/CMPVAL'.Comparison data (CMPVAL)
:P.The comparison data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Compare value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 80 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Starting position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 80.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/PGM'.Program to call (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SBSD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the subsystem description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/MAXACT'.Maximum active routing steps (MAXACT)
:P.The most jobs or routing steps that can be active at once. *NOMAX
sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/POOLID'.Storage pool identifier (POOLID)
:P.The subsystem pool identifier.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/THDRSCAFN'.Thread resources affinity (THDRSCAFN)
:P.Whether the job's secondary threads are kept close to the processors
and memory the first thread uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Group
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOGROUP, *GROUP.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRTGE/RSCAFNGRP'.Resources affinity group (RSCAFNGRP)
:P.Whether the job's threads are kept together on the same processor
group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSBSD.Change Subsystem Description (CHGSBSD)
:P.Use the Change Subsystem Description (CHGSBSD) command to change a
subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSBSD/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSBSD/POOLS'.Storage pools (POOLS)
:P.The storage pools for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pool identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Storage size or name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Activity level
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSBSD/MAXJOBS'.Maximum jobs (MAXJOBS)
:P.The most jobs allowed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSBSD/SGNDSPF'.Sign-on display file (SGNDSPF)
:P.The sign-on display file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSBSD/SYSLIBLE'.Subsystem library (SYSLIBLE)
:P.The subsystem library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSBSD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSHRPOOL.Change Shared Storage Pool (CHGSHRPOOL)
:P.Use the Change Shared Storage Pool (CHGSHRPOOL) command to change the
size, activity level and tuning of a shared storage pool.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/POOL'.Shared pool (POOL)
:P.The shared pool for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:PT.:PK.*INTERACT:EPK.
:PD.Interactive jobs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MACHINE, *SPOOL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/SIZE'.Storage size (SIZE)
:P.The storage size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 32 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/ACTLVL'.Activity level (ACTLVL)
:P.The activity level for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/PAGING'.Paging option (PAGING)
:P.The paging option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*FIXED:EPK.
:PD.Fixed length.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/PTY'.Priority (PTY)
:P.The priority for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 14.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/MINPCT'.Minimum size percent (MINPCT)
:P.The minimum size percent for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 100.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/MAXPCT'.Maximum size percent (MAXPCT)
:P.The maximum size percent for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 1 to 100.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/MINFAULT'.Minimum faults (MINFAULT)
:P.The minimum faults for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/PERFAULT'.Per-thread faults (PERFAULT)
:P.The per-thread faults for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSHRPOOL/MAXFAULT'.Maximum faults (MAXFAULT)
:P.The maximum faults for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 2 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 9999.99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSYSLIBL.Change System Library List (CHGSYSLIBL)
:P.Use the Change System Library List (CHGSYSLIBL) command to add a
library to, or remove one from, the system part of the library list of
the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSYSLIBL/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSYSLIBL/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REMOVE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLRJOBQ.Clear Job Queue (CLRJOBQ)
:P.Use the Clear Job Queue (CLRJOBQ) command to remove every job waiting
on a job queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRJOBQ/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTCLS.Create Class (CRTCLS)
:P.Use the Create Class (CRTCLS) command to create a class.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/RUNPTY'.Run priority (RUNPTY)
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 50 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/TIMESLICE'.Time slice (TIMESLICE)
:P.How long, in milliseconds, a thread of the job runs before another
thread of the same priority gets the processor.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 2000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/PURGE'.Eligible for purge (PURGE)
:P.Whether the job may be moved out of main storage when it waits for a
long time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/DFTWAIT'.Default wait time (DFTWAIT)
:P.How many seconds the system waits for an instruction to complete
before it signals a time-out.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/CPUTIME'.Maximum CPU time (CPUTIME)
:P.The maximum CPU time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/MAXTMPSTG'.Maximum temporary storage (MAXTMPSTG)
:P.The maximum temporary storage for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/MAXTHD'.Maximum threads (MAXTHD)
:P.The maximum threads for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTCLS/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTJOBD.Create Job Description (CRTJOBD)
:P.Use the Create Job Description (CRTJOBD) command to create a job
description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/JOBPTY'.Job priority (on JOBQ) (JOBPTY)
:P.The priority of the job on the job queue, from 1 (highest) to 9
(lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 5 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/OUTPTY'.Output priority (on OUTQ) (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 5 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/PRTDEV'.Print device (PRTDEV)
:P.The printer device the spooled output prints on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/ACGCDE'.Accounting code (ACGCDE)
:P.The accounting code the job's resources are charged to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/RTGDTA'.Routing data (RTGDTA)
:P.The routing data the subsystem compares with its routing entries to
choose the program the job runs.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 80 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RQSDTA.
:P.When no value is given, QCMDI is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/RQSDTA'.Request data (RQSDTA)
:P.The request data placed on the job's message queue for the program to
read.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/SYNTAX'.CL syntax check severity (SYNTAX)
:P.The CL syntax check severity for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCHK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/INLLIBL'.Initial library list (INLLIBL)
:P.The initial user part of the library list of the job.
:P.Up to 250 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/ENDSEV'.End severity (ENDSEV)
:P.The end severity for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/LOG'.Message logging (LOG)
:P.The message logging for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 4.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 4 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Severity
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Text
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/LOGCLPGM'.Log CL program commands (LOGCLPGM)
:P.Whether the commands that CL programs run are written to the job log.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/LOGOUTPUT'.Log output (LOGOUTPUT)
:P.When the job log is produced as a spooled file&colon. by the job
itself at its end, by a server job afterwards, or not at all.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBLOGSVR, *JOBEND, *PND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/INQMSGRPY'.Inquiry message reply (INQMSGRPY)
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYSRPYL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/HOLD'.Hold on job queue (HOLD)
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It is not held.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/DATE'.Job date (DATE)
:P.The job date.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/SWS'.Job switches (SWS)
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 00000000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/JOBMSGQMX'.Job message queue maximum (JOBMSGQMX)
:P.The largest size of the job's message queue, in megabytes.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 2 to 64.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/JOBMSGQFL'.Job message queue full action (JOBMSGQFL)
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NOWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, no more messages are added.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*PRTWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the messages are printed and the queue starts over.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/DEVRCYACN'.Device recovery action (DEVRCYACN)
:P.What happens to the job when its display device has an error&colon. a
message is sent, the request is ended, or the job is ended.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DSCMSG, *DSCENDRQS, *ENDJOB, *ENDJOBNOLIST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/TSEPOOL'.Time slice end pool (TSEPOOL)
:P.Whether the job moves to the base pool when its time slice ends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/SPLFACN'.Spooled file action (SPLFACN)
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DETACH:EPK.
:PD.Detached from the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/DDMCNV'.DDM conversation (DDMCNV)
:P.Whether conversations to remote systems for DDM are kept or dropped
when nothing is using them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DROP:EPK.
:PD.Dropped.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/ALWMLTTHD'.Allow multiple threads (ALWMLTTHD)
:P.Whether to allow multiple threads.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBD/INLASPGRP'.Initial ASP group (INLASPGRP)
:P.The initial ASP group for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTJOBQ.Create Job Queue (CRTJOBQ)
:P.Use the Create Job Queue (CRTJOBQ) command to create a job queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBQ/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBQ/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBQ/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBQ/AUTCHK'.Authority to check (AUTCHK)
:P.Which authority is checked&colon. the owner's, or data authority.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAAUT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJOBQ/OPRCTL'.Operator controlled (OPRCTL)
:P.Whether users with job control special authority can control the
queue.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
