:HELP NAME=DSPBCKSTS.Display Backup Status (DSPBCKSTS)
:P.The Display Backup Status (DSPBCKSTS) command works with the backups
that ran.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPBCKSTS/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPBCKUP.Display Backup Options (DSPBCKUP)
:P.Use the Display Backup Options (DSPBCKUP) command to show a backup's
