:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPLIBL.Display Library List (DSPLIBL)
:P.Use the Display Library List (DSPLIBL) command to display the library
list of the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLIBL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSBSD.Display Subsystem Description (DSPSBSD)
:P.Use the Display Subsystem Description (DSPSBSD) command to display a
subsystem description and its entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT, *OPRATR, *POOLS, *AJE, *WSNAME,
*WSTYPE, *JOBQ, *RTGE, *CMNE, *RMTLOCNAME, *PJE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=EDTLIBL.Edit Library List (EDTLIBL)
:P.Use the Edit Library List (EDTLIBL) command to edit the user part of
the library list on a display.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDCLNUP.End Cleanup (ENDCLNUP)
:P.Use the End Cleanup (ENDCLNUP) command to stop the daily cleanup.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDJOB.End Job (ENDJOB)
:P.Use the End Job (ENDJOB) command to end a job, controlled or at once.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/OPTION'.How to end (OPTION)
:P.The how to end for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/DELAY'.Controlled end delay time (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/SPLFILE'.Delete spooled files (SPLFILE)
:P.Whether to delete spooled files.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/LOGLMT'.Maximum log entries (LOGLMT)
:P.The maximum log entries for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/ADLINTJOBS'.Additional interactive jobs (ADLINTJOBS)
:P.The additional interactive jobs for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *GRPJOB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJOB/DUPJOBOPT'.Duplicate job option (DUPJOBOPT)
:P.What happens when more than one job matches the name given&colon.
show a list to choose from, or send a message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDSBS.End Subsystem (ENDSBS)
:P.Use the End Subsystem (ENDSBS) command to end one subsystem or all of
them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSBS/SBS'.Subsystem (SBS)
:P.The subsystem for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSBS/OPTION'.How to end (OPTION)
:P.The how to end for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSBS/DELAY'.Controlled end delay time (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOLIMIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSBS/ENDSBSOPT'.End subsystem option (ENDSBSOPT)
:P.The end subsystem option for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOJOBLOG, *CHGPTY, *CHGTSL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSBS/BCHTIMLMT'.Batch time limit (BCHTIMLMT)
:P.The batch time limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDSYS.End System (ENDSYS)
:P.Use the End System (ENDSYS) command to end every subsystem but the
controlling one, which leaves only the console job&colon. the restricted
state.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSYS/OPTION'.How to end (OPTION)
:P.The how to end for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSYS/DELAY'.Controlled end delay time (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOLIMIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSYS/ENDSBSOPT'.End subsystem option (ENDSBSOPT)
:P.The end subsystem option for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOJOBLOG, *CHGPTY, *CHGTSL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSYS/BCHTIMLMT'.Batch time limit (BCHTIMLMT)
:P.The batch time limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLDJOB.Hold Job (HLDJOB)
:P.Use the Hold Job (HLDJOB) command to hold a job, and its spooled
files if asked.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDJOB/SPLFILE'.Hold spooled files (SPLFILE)
:P.Whether to hold spooled files.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDJOB/DUPJOBOPT'.Duplicate job option (DUPJOBOPT)
:P.What happens when more than one job matches the name given&colon.
show a list to choose from, or send a message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLDJOBQ.Hold Job Queue (HLDJOBQ)
:P.Use the Hold Job Queue (HLDJOBQ) command to hold a job queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDJOBQ/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLDJOBSCDE.Hold Job Schedule Entry (HLDJOBSCDE)
:P.Use the Hold Job Schedule Entry (HLDJOBSCDE) command to hold entries
of the job schedule.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDJOBSCDE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='HLDJOBSCDE/ENTRYNBR'.Entry number (ENTRYNBR)
:P.The entry number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTSYSINF.Print System Information (PRTSYSINF)
:P.Use the Print System Information (PRTSYSINF) command to print what a
recovery needs to know about the system.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PWRDWNSYS.Power Down System (PWRDWNSYS)
:P.Use the Power Down System (PWRDWNSYS) command to end every subsystem
and power the system down, with an IPL afterwards if asked.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/OPTION'.How to end (OPTION)
:P.The how to end for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/DELAY'.Controlled end delay time (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOLIMIT.
:P.When no value is given, 3600 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/RESTART'.Restart (RESTART)
:P.The restart for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Restart after power down
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Restart type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IPLA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/IPLSRC'.IPL source (IPLSRC)
:P.The IPL source for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PANEL, *IMGCLG.
:P.The value must be A, B, D.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/ENDSBSOPT'.End subsystem option (ENDSBSOPT)
:P.The end subsystem option for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOJOBLOG, *CHGPTY, *CHGTSL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/TIMOUTOPT'.Timeout option (TIMOUTOPT)
:P.The timeout option for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONTINUE, *POWEROFF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PWRDWNSYS/CONFIRM'.Confirm (CONFIRM)
:P.Whether to confirm.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSBCKUP.Backup Plan (QSBCKUP)
:P.Use the Backup Plan (QSBCKUP) command to RUNBCKUP's steps from the
service, and their outcome back.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSBCKUP/ACTION'.Action (ACTION)
:P.The action for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PLAN, *DONE, *SETDFT, *FIELDS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSBCKUP/BCKUPOPT'.Backup options (BCKUPOPT)
:P.The backup options of the operational assistant&colon. daily, weekly
or monthly.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *NONE is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSBCKUP/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *BCKUPOPT is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSBCKUP/DATA'.Data (DATA)
:P.The data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *NONE is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSMNRST.Restore Menu Option (QSMNRST)
:P.Use the Restore Menu Option (QSMNRST) command to GO RESTORE options
21 to 23.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSMNRST/OPTION'.GO RESTORE option (OPTION)
:P.The GO RESTORE option for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value must be '21', '22', '23'.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSMNSAVE.Save Menu Option (QSMNSAVE)
:P.Use the Save Menu Option (QSMNSAVE) command to GO SAVE options 20 to
23.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSMNSAVE/OPTION'.GO SAVE option (OPTION)
:P.The GO SAVE option for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value must be '20', '21', '22', '23'.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSPMTOVR.Prompt Override Values (QSPMTOVR)
:P.The Prompt Override Values (QSPMTOVR) command works with a command's
current values, for its prompt override.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSPMTOVR/CMD'.Command (CMD)
:P.The command for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSPMTOVR/KEY'.Key parameters (KEY)
:P.The key parameters for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *NONE is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RLSJOB.Release Job (RLSJOB)
:P.Use the Release Job (RLSJOB) command to release a held job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSJOB/DUPJOBOPT'.Duplicate job option (DUPJOBOPT)
:P.What happens when more than one job matches the name given&colon.
show a list to choose from, or send a message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RLSJOBQ.Release Job Queue (RLSJOBQ)
:P.Use the Release Job Queue (RLSJOBQ) command to release a held job
queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSJOBQ/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RLSJOBSCDE.Release Job Schedule Entry (RLSJOBSCDE)
:P.Use the Release Job Schedule Entry (RLSJOBSCDE) command to release
held entries of the job schedule.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RLSJOBSCDE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
