:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVJOBSCDE.Remove Job Schedule Entry (RMVJOBSCDE)
:P.Use the Remove Job Schedule Entry (RMVJOBSCDE) command to remove
entries from the job schedule.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJOBSCDE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJOBSCDE/ENTRYNBR'.Entry number (ENTRYNBR)
:P.The entry number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVLIBLE.Remove Library List Entry (RMVLIBLE)
:P.Use the Remove Library List Entry (RMVLIBLE) command to remove a
library from the user part of the library list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLIBLE/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVPJE.Remove Prestart Job Entry (RMVPJE)
:P.Use the Remove Prestart Job Entry (RMVPJE) command to remove a
prestart job entry from a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPJE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPJE/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVRTGE.Remove Routing Entry (RMVRTGE)
:P.Use the Remove Routing Entry (RMVRTGE) command to remove a routing
entry from a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVRTGE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVRTGE/SEQNBR'.Routing entry sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The routing entry sequence number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVWSE.Remove Work Station Entry (RMVWSE)
:P.Use the Remove Work Station Entry (RMVWSE) command to remove a
workstation entry from a subsystem description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVWSE/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVWSE/WRKSTN'.Work station name (WRKSTN)
:P.The work station name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVWSE/WRKSTNTYPE'.Work station type (WRKSTNTYPE)
:P.The work station type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NONASCII.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RUNBCKUP.Run Backup (RUNBCKUP)
:P.Use the Run Backup (RUNBCKUP) command to run a backup with its
options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNBCKUP/BCKUPOPT'.Backup options (BCKUPOPT)
:P.The backup options of the operational assistant&colon. daily, weekly
or monthly.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WEEKLY:EPK.
:PD.Weekly.
:PT.:PK.*MONTHLY:EPK.
:PD.Monthly.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DAILY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RUNBCKUP/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BCKUPOPT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SBMJOB.Submit Job (SBMJOB)
:P.Use the Submit Job (SBMJOB) command to submit a command to run as a
batch job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/CMD'.Command to run (CMD)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/JOBD'.Job description (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/JOBPTY'.Job priority (on JOBQ) (JOBPTY)
:P.The priority of the job on the job queue, from 1 (highest) to 9
(lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/OUTPTY'.Output priority (on OUTQ) (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/PRTDEV'.Print device (PRTDEV)
:P.The printer device the spooled output prints on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/OUTQ'.Output queue (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/PRTTXT'.Print text (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/RTGDTA'.Routing data (RTGDTA)
:P.The routing data the subsystem compares with its routing entries to
choose the program the job runs.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 80 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RQSDTA.
:P.When no value is given, QCMDB is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/RQSDTA'.Request data (RQSDTA)
:P.The request data placed on the job's message queue for the program to
read.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the command.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/SYSLIBL'.System library list (SYSLIBL)
:P.The system library list for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/CURLIB'.Current library (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CRTDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/INLLIBL'.Initial library list (INLLIBL)
:P.The initial user part of the library list of the job.
:P.Up to 250 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/LOG'.Message logging (LOG)
:P.The message logging for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Level
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 4.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 4 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Severity
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Text
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PK.*SECLVL:EPK.
:PD.With the second-level text of the messages.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/LOGCLPGM'.Log CL program commands (LOGCLPGM)
:P.Whether the commands that CL programs run are written to the job log.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/LOGOUTPUT'.Log output (LOGOUTPUT)
:P.When the job log is produced as a spooled file&colon. by the job
itself at its end, by a server job afterwards, or not at all.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBLOGSVR, *JOBEND, *PND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/JOBMSGQMX'.Job message queue maximum (JOBMSGQMX)
:P.The largest size of the job's message queue, in megabytes.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 2 to 64.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/JOBMSGQFL'.Job message queue full action (JOBMSGQFL)
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NOWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, no more messages are added.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*PRTWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the messages are printed and the queue starts over.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/INQMSGRPY'.Inquiry message reply (INQMSGRPY)
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYSRPYL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/HOLD'.Hold on job queue (HOLD)
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It is not held.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/SCDDATE'.Schedule date (SCDDATE)
:P.The date the job is scheduled to run.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MONTHSTR, *MONTHEND, *MON, *TUE, *WED, *THU,
*FRI, *SAT, *SUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/SCDTIME'.Schedule time (SCDTIME)
:P.The time the job is scheduled to run.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/DATE'.Job date (DATE)
:P.The job date.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/SWS'.Job switches (SWS)
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/DSPSBMJOB'.Allow display by WRKSBMJOB (DSPSBMJOB)
:P.Whether to allow display by WRKSBMJOB.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the workstation.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.No message queue&colon. messages are not sent.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDUNQ:EPK.
:PD.The unique-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. every
character has its own weight.
:PT.:PK.*LANGIDSHR:EPK.
:PD.The shared-weight sort sequence of the language&colon. upper and
lower case compare equal.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/LANGID'.Language ID (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/CNTRYID'.Country or region ID (CNTRYID)
:P.The country or region identifier&colon. two letters.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/CPYENVVAR'.Copy environment variables (CPYENVVAR)
:P.Whether to copy environment variables.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/ALWMLTTHD'.Allow multiple threads (ALWMLTTHD)
:P.Whether to allow multiple threads.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/SPLFACN'.Spooled file action (SPLFACN)
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DETACH:EPK.
:PD.Detached from the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SBMJOB/DDMCNV'.DDM conversation (DDMCNV)
:P.Whether conversations to remote systems for DDM are kept or dropped
when nothing is using them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DROP:EPK.
:PD.Dropped.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SIGNOFF.Sign Off (SIGNOFF)
:P.Use the Sign Off (SIGNOFF) command to end the interactive job and
show the sign-on display.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNOFF/LOG'.Job log (LOG)
:P.The job log for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNOFF/DROP'.Drop line (DROP)
:P.The drop line for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNOFF/ENDCNN'.End connection (ENDCNN)
:P.Whether to end connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRCLNUP.Start Cleanup (STRCLNUP)
:P.Use the Start Cleanup (STRCLNUP) command to schedule the daily
cleanup, or run it now.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCLNUP/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SCHED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRSBS.Start Subsystem (STRSBS)
:P.Use the Start Subsystem (STRSBS) command to start a subsystem from
its description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSBS/SBSD'.Subsystem description (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TFRJOB.Transfer Job (TFRJOB)
:P.Use the Transfer Job (TFRJOB) command to transfer the interactive job
to another job queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TFRJOB/JOBQ'.Job queue (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TFRJOB/RTGDTA'.Routing data (RTGDTA)
:P.The routing data the subsystem compares with its routing entries to
choose the program the job runs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job description.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 80 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RQSDTA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKACTJOB.Work with Active Jobs (WRKACTJOB)
:P.Use the Work with Active Jobs (WRKACTJOB) command to work with the
active jobs and their statistics.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/RESET'.Reset statistics (RESET)
:P.Whether to reset statistics.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/SBS'.Subsystem (SBS)
:P.The subsystem for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/CPUPCTLMT'.CPU percent limit (CPUPCTLMT)
:P.The CPU percent limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 99.9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/RSPLMT'.Response time limit (RSPLMT)
:P.The response time limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
The value must be from 0 to 999.9.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/SEQ'.Sequence (SEQ)
:P.The sequence for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SBS, *CPUPCT, *FUNCTION, *IOTOTAL, *POOL, *PTY,
*RSP, *STS, *TYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJOB/INTERVAL'.Interval (INTERVAL)
:P.The interval for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 5 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKCLS.Work with Classes (WRKCLS)
:P.Use the Work with Classes (WRKCLS) command to work with classes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCLS/CLS'.Class (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
