:HELP NAME='WRKSBSJOB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSHRPOOL.Work with Shared Pools (WRKSHRPOOL)
:P.Use the Work with Shared Pools (WRKSHRPOOL) command to work with the
shared storage pools.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSHRPOOL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSYSACT.Work with System Activity (WRKSYSACT)
:P.Use the Work with System Activity (WRKSYSACT) command to work with
the system activity, jobs and tasks by processor use.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSACT/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PK.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSACT/INTERVAL'.Interval, seconds (INTERVAL)
:P.The interval, seconds for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 5 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSACT/INFTYPE'.Information type (INFTYPE)
:P.The information type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBTASK, *TASK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSACT/SEQ'.Sequence (SEQ)
:P.The sequence for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CPU, *IO.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSACT/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QPFRDATA is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSACT/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QAITMON is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSYSSTS.Work with System Status (WRKSYSSTS)
:P.Use the Work with System Status (WRKSYSSTS) command to work with the
system status and the storage pools.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSSTS/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSSTS/RESET'.Reset statistics (RESET)
:P.Whether to reset statistics.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSSTS/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:PT.:PK.*ADVANCED:EPK.
:PD.Advanced assistance&colon. the system displays with more on each and
fewer keys shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKUSRJOB.Work with User Jobs (WRKUSRJOB)
:P.Use the Work with User Jobs (WRKUSRJOB) command to work with the jobs
of a user.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ACTIVE:EPK.
:PD.Active.
:PT.:PK.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.The value of the output queue.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBQ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/JOBTYPE'.Job type (JOBTYPE)
:P.The job type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*INTERACT:EPK.
:PD.Interactive jobs.
:PT.:PK.*BATCH:EPK.
:PD.Batch jobs.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
